<title>DENMARK: Jyske Bank 1996 pre-tax profits up.</title>
<headline>Jyske Bank 1996 pre-tax profits up.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	    (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit before tax and extraordinary items  993  vs   961</p>
<p> Group profit after tax			   645  vs   725</p>
<p> Losses and bad debt provisions		 346  vs   382</p>
<p> Securities and forex results		   406  vs   491</p>
<p> Net interest and fees income		 2,205  vs 2,250</p>
<p> Result of financial items		    2,803  vs 2,954</p>
<p> Operating expenses,depreciation	    1,528  vs 1,460</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (percent)		     10  vs     8</p>
<p> Capital ratio (percent)			   12.2vs    13</p>
<p>Own capital end-1996  4.432 billion vs 3.874 billion end-1995</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Danish banking group is Jyske Bank A/S, Denmark's fourth biggest bank. It said in a statement that it expected core earnings before securities income, extraordinary items and tax of between 600 and 750 million crowns in 1997, compared to 657 million in 1996.</p>
<p>The 1996 pre-tax result was above analysts' expectations of 985 million crowns.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom + 45-33-969650</p>
